Bag with receipt 
This project involves implementing a `ReceiptBag` program in C++. 
The `ReceiptBag` stores data items and assigns a unique receipt number 
to each, allowing for the subsequent removal of specific items.The program 
supports various data types (such as numbers and strings) and utilizes a `vector` 
container to store the data items alongside their corresponding receipt numbers.Key 
functionalities include `insert()`, `remove()`, `contains()`, `size()`, and `isEmpty()`. 
The `insert()` function adds items and assigns receipt numbers, while the `remove()` function 
deletes items based on their receipt numbers, raising an error if an invalid number is provided.Additionally,
I developed several test cases to verify the program's correctness. These tests cover ensuring receipt number uniqueness,
correctly removing items, triggering error messages for invalid numbers, and accurately calculating the container size.In summary,
this project demonstrates the application of C++ classes, templates, `vector` containers, and testing methodologies. The `ReceiptBag` program 
successfully stores data items and enables effective management through the use of receipt numbers.